.Dd @NCOLLECTD_DATE@
.Dt NCOLLECTD-NSD 5
.Os ncollectd @NCOLLECTD_VERSION@
.Sh NAME
.Nm ncollectd-nsd
.Nd Documentation of ncollectd's nsd plugin
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -compact
\fBload-plugin\fP nsd
\fBplugin\fP nsd {
    \fBinstance\fP \fIname\fP {
        \fBhost\fP \fIhost\fP
        \fBport\fP \fIport\fP
        \fBsocket-path\fP \fIpath\fP
        \fBserver-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
        \fBcontrol-key\fP \fIfile\fP
        \fBcontrol-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
        \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBlabel\fP \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
        \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
        \fBfilter\fP {
            ...
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The \fBnsd\fP plugin collect metrics from the NSD authoritative DNS Name Server.
.Pp
The configuration consists of one or more \fBinstance\fP blocks:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \fBhost\fP \fIhost\fP
Hostname to connect.
.It \fBport\fP \fIport\fP
Port to connect.
.It \fBsocket-path\fP \fIpath\fP
Path of the NSD control unix socket. If set, \fBhost\fP and \fBport\fP are ignored.
.It \fBserver-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
Server certificate used to verify the server.
Defaults to \fI/etc/nsd/nsd_server.pem\fP.
.It \fBcontrol-key\fP \fIfile\fP
Private key of the client.
Defaults to \fI/etc/nsd/nsd_control.key\fP.
.It \fBcontrol-cert\fP \fIfile\fP
Certificate of the client.
Defaults to \fI/etc/nsd/nsd_control.pem\fP.
.Pp
TLS is used when the \fBhost\fP is not a local address or when any of
\fBserver-cert\fP, \fBcontrol-key\fP or \fBcontrol-cert\fP is set.
.It \fBtimeout\fP \fIseconds\fP
Timeout for the send and receive operations with the server.
By default half of the \fBinterval\fP is used.
.It \fBserver-name\fP \fIservername\fP
.It \fBlabel\fP \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
Append the label \fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP to the submitting metrics.
.It \fBinterval\fP \fIseconds\fP
Sets the interval (in seconds) in which the values will be collected
from this instance.
.It \fBfilter\fP
Configure a filter to modify or drop the metrics.
See \fBFILTER CONFIGURATION\fP in
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5 .
.El
.Sh "SEE ALSO"
.Xr ncollectd 1 ,
.Xr ncollectd.conf 5
